{title: When We All Get to Heaven}
{artist: Eliza E. Hewitt / Emily D. Wilson}
{genre: Gospel}
{style: Upbeat}
{flow: Closing}
{key: C}
{tempo: 113}
{time: 4/4}
{c: Chords checked against the four-part harmony of the Cyber Hymnal score (Tabernacle Hymns Number Three (Chicago, Illinois: Tabernacle Publishing, 1950), # 51)}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]Sing the wondrous love of Jesus,
[G7]Sing His mercy and His [C]grace.
[C]In the mansions [F]bright and blessèd
[C]He’ll pre[F]pare for [G7]us a [C]place.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C]When we all get to Heaven,
[C]What a [Am]day of re[D7]joicing that will [G7]be!
[G7]When we [C7]all see [F]Jesus,
[F]We’ll [C]sing [G7]and shout the victo[C]ry!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]While we walk the pilgrim pathway,
[G7]Clouds will overspread the [C]sky;
[C]But when traveling [F]days are over,
[C]Not a [F]shadow, [G7]not a [C]sigh.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]Let us then be true and faithful,
[G7]Trusting, serving every [C]day;
[C]Just one glimpse of [F]Him in glory
[C]Will the [F]toils of [G7]life re[C]pay.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[C]Onward to the prize before us!
[G7]Soon His beauty we’ll be[C]hold;
[C]Soon the pearly [F]gates will open;
[C]We shall [F]tread the [G7]streets of [C]gold.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
